-- Replaces the hackathon bounding-box placeholders from migration 003 with
-- real IGAD member-state boundaries.
--
-- Source: Natural Earth 1:10m Admin 0 Countries (public domain),
-- https://github.com/nvkelso/natural-earth-vector, simplified to ~100 m.
--
-- Bounding boxes made the compound-risk choropleth render as rectangles over
-- Africa, and made ST_Intersects country attribution wrong near every border:
-- Kenya's box, for example, covered parts of Tanzania and Somalia.
--
-- 1:10m rather than 1:50m because coastal accuracy matters here: at 1:50m the
-- generalised coastline put Djibouti City ~2 km offshore, resolving to no
-- country at all.
--
-- Note that no generalised dataset attributes every coastal point: Mombasa
-- Island sits ~1 km outside Natural Earth's Kenya polygon even at full 1:10m.
-- Country lookups therefore fall back to the nearest country within a few km
-- rather than relying on strict containment (see repositories/spatial.py).
--
-- Each country is its ISO_A2_EH feature unioned with any territory Natural
-- Earth lists separately under the same ADM0_ISO but with no ISO_A2. That
-- matters for Somaliland: excluding it would leave a hole over Hargeisa where
-- alerts resolved to no country and SO subscribers were never matched.
--
-- Only geom is updated; iso2 and name are left as migration 003 seeded them.

-- DJ: Djibouti
